[{:db/id "q-43775/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "7f9c2965-7363-58d3-89d4-4097be2345bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43775/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "346c2b38-29ab-5943-9356-a400c89b5989" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43775/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "1ba3eac0-5f8a-5c01-9f72-7ef3bb99605b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43775/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "355ac00f-d608-5fd2-a380-3f900ec90bc5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43775/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "1a32d547-e346-5f3f-9a38-aa15ddbc48ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43775/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "acb674f6-5ce2-5c57-80fb-790190517c2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43775/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer-field/choices ["q-43775/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-43775/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-43775/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-43775/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-43775/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43775" :question/id #uuid "60087cbe-41e4-5844-91aa-1e5069d8dad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-43775" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $E$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\alpha A$ where $A$ is some fixed $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\alpha \\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $E$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}={\\alpha }_{1}A$ and ${A}_{2}={\\alpha }_{2}A$ are two matrices from $E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & ={\\alpha }_{1}A+{\\alpha }_{2}A=({\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{2})A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $B=\\alpha A$ is an element of $E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k\\alpha A=(k\\alpha )A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-43775/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43775"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "54ce6988-a042-5a66-bc3c-fbe0f3341d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f344ef99-3654-5695-af8d-ced117ae3ed4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "2343f30f-cf63-55b0-8f2c-84f7a4da0c24" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "2365f2d5-97c0-549b-8449-1645ed496ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "4ffdb35a-0985-5355-a6af-17aa541cc0b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a2eb041b-086c-5fa3-9789-a8d848551c8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94380/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer-field/choices ["q-94380/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-94380/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-94380/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-94380/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-94380/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94380" :question/id #uuid "e1f3a490-989c-5c43-8660-5db51b62310c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94380" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[-5,0]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-5,0]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[-5,0]\\,|\\,f(0)=0}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $B$ is closed under function addition\n- $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $B$ is a subspace of $C[-5,0]$\n- $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-5,0]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is  true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in B$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(0) & =kf(0) \\\\  & =k\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $B$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94380/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94380"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "e12fbf74-305a-5c82-a847-3968c53f6116" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "c66c6547-993f-5602-82a0-b7f332428e60" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "9feb8f2f-4d8c-551c-a50b-4bc356f78e95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "9644ad1a-de21-547c-b426-16ac4ee3dff9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "9d78cdcc-a214-5760-88d0-befcef5f983e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15338ece-a3d5-5ad7-b8e8-4bd9f637bd25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107112/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer-field/choices ["q-107112/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-107112/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-107112/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-107112/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-107112/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107112" :question/id #uuid "60eef387-3891-5b06-9190-577fe6b6981a" :question/math-academy-id "q-107112" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C={[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a\\in R}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & -ka\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107112/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107112"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "086e4b43-fecd-5ade-96e5-324132e8528e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "3f7046a8-8aa6-50b5-8b81-69154f408f01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "5bd29fc3-0eac-5599-844d-2ec3a8dffc67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "f2512662-56ce-5a3a-a8c7-993127cb6087" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "0e4ed195-fdfd-5512-a815-9f6efa29a4dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93360677-739a-5139-87b0-a1cc9358dd16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107113/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer-field/choices ["q-107113/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-107113/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-107113/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-107113/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-107113/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107113" :question/id #uuid "6511708a-ae52-5c53-bdf3-d211b27f9e51" :question/math-academy-id "q-107113" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107113/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f306cf2-6881-5948-90bd-4e0ce98b4116"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "6f0f2c2e-b16f-581c-8673-d8bf47534538" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "953be217-94d5-5eba-b620-b976e7c12eb0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "e38f61a9-9a2b-58b0-a88f-5fa46f67b022" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" :answer/id #uuid "d4d701f0-394c-5884-9f25-a3b3d23e226c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "399bb6cc-edd7-51ab-b165-8af9903ad686" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "26b23c42-1774-5dee-8c35-7f1af2c9c89d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107143/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer-field/choices ["q-107143/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-107143/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-107143/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-107143/selection/a93f071c9e37df87ddd39fa5ca5c1b993bc7a9722336877075659d8a831d9910" "q-107143/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107143" :question/id #uuid "b507c1f4-d8e7-5cb2-9ef0-485dee50d613" :question/math-academy-id "q-107143" :question/problem "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $M$ containing all functions that return an integer value at $x=1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $M$ is closed under function addition\n- $M$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $M$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $M$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are functions from $M,$ then $f(1)$  and  $g(1)$ are integers and so $(f+g)(1)=f(1)+g(1)$ must be an integer number too. So, $M$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, $f(x)=1$ is a function in $M$, but $0.5f(x)$ is not in $M$ because\n$(0.5f)(1)=0.5\\cdot f(1)=0.5$ is not an integer. So, $M$ is *not*  closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $M$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-107143/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107143"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
